WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.670
In 1965, coal supplied 59 per cent
of all the energy used in the UK.

2
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:08.810
Then the line falls.

3
00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:13.170
By 2024, coal's share
was just 2.5 per cent.

4
00:00:13.220 --> 00:00:18.950
That autumn, Britain's last coal power
station, Ratcliffe-on-Soar, closed.

5
00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:21.210
So what took coal's place?

6
00:00:21.260 --> 00:00:22.250
Nuclear power?

7
00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:23.170
Oil?

8
00:00:23.220 --> 00:00:23.990
Something else?

9
00:00:24.040 --> 00:00:27.210
In this mission, you'll find
out what an energy mix is,

10
00:00:27.260 --> 00:00:29.390
and read the UK's from a chart.

11
00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:33.630
Then you'll trace how the
mix has shifted since 1970,

12
00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:35.390
one source at a time.

13
00:00:35.440 --> 00:00:39.470
Your mission: find out what has
replaced coal in Britain's energy.
